				949,
				2
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Extract generic RPC Request and Response envelopes\n\nCreate dedicated `Request.rs` and `Response.rs` files within `Source/RPC/Types` to house the generic `Struct<T>` envelope definitions. Previously, these fundamental types were likely defined inline or less explicitly, cluttering the module root.\n\nThis change aligns the `Types` module with the project-wide file-per-struct convention recently enforced across `Workspace`, `Track`, `RunTime`, and `Vine` modules. By isolating these generic envelopes, we ensure consistent PascalCase file paths and prepare the RPC layer for stricter symbol resolution required by Tauri's `generate_handler!` macro and future gRPC integration.",
			"SHA": "913bd697f08b682fcf01826de7d17a336e5e710a"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-02T05:15:55Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				946,
				2
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Extract Vine connection and status DTOs to dedicated files\n\nDecompose the `Source/RPC/Vine` module to align with the project-wide PascalCase file-per-struct convention. Extract the `VineConnectionInfo` struct and `VineServiceStatus` enum from the monolithic module definition into `VineConnectionInfo.rs` and `VineServiceStatus.rs` respectively.\n\nEach new file defines its core type as `Struct` or `Enum` to satisfy Tauri's `generate_handler!` macro symbol resolution requirements when referenced via the full module path. This change mirrors the architectural pattern recently applied to Workspace, Track, and RunTime modules, ensuring consistent IPC layer structure for the Vine gRPC protocol definitions.",
			"SHA": "a4de592894642b94e50f6b998a952fef92bb47fb"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-02T05:14:44Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				943,
				3
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Decompose Workspace RPC module into file-per-struct submodules\n\nRefactor `Source/RPC/Workspace/WorkspaceService.rs` to align with the project-wide PascalCase module path convention. Replace the monolithic file containing inline struct definitions with explicit `pub mod` delegates to `TextDocumentInfo.rs`, `WorkspaceFolder.rs`, and `WorkspaceService.rs`.\n\nThe `TextDocumentInfo` and `WorkspaceFolder` DTOs are extracted into their own files, while the `WorkspaceService` struct and its constructor logic reside in a dedicated service file. All files use the `Struct` naming pattern within their respective modules to satisfy Tauri's `generate_handler!` macro requirements for symbol resolution. This establishes a consistent architectural pattern for the Workspace service layer, mirroring recent refactors in the Track, RunTime, and Effect modules.",
			"SHA": "40ceefb085721173ab4c1874a30b3070470ab4aa"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-02T05:08:42Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				939,
				12
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Decompose RPC modules into file-per-struct submodules\n\nRefactor all `Source/RPC/*.rs` files to align with the project-wide PascalCase module path convention enforced in recent `Track` and `RunTime` refactors. Replace inline struct definitions and `pub use` re-exports with explicit `pub mod` declarations that delegate to sibling files (e.g., `CommandService.rs`, `EchoActionServer.rs`).\n\nThis change ensures that every struct and implementation resides in a file matching its PascalCase name, allowing Tauri's `generate_handler!` macro to correctly resolve `__cmd__` symbols via the full module path. Placeholder services (Debug, Processes, SCM, Terminals, Windows) are updated to use the `Struct` naming pattern within their feature gates, while active services (Commands, Configuration, EchoAction, Telemetry, Workspace, Types, Vine) are split into their constituent DTOs and service handles. The `EchoAction` module retains its complex logic but now delegates to dedicated sub-files for `EchoActionServer`, `ExtensionHostRegistry`, `ExtensionRouter`, and priority resolution.\n\nThis establishes a consistent architectural pattern across the entire RPC layer, eliminating flat imports and ensuring strict path resolution for IPC generation.",
			"SHA": "6816476bd1c4c5f0047725acc343bcdfe592a750"
		}
	],
